# The OTA package set — one name per line, `#` comments and blank lines ignored.
#
# This list is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH, read by:
#   scripts/publish-ota-repo.sh    — what gets copied into the signed repo
#   scripts/verify-ota-parity.sh   — what the release gate compares
#
# It exists because the set used to live only inside publish-ota-repo.sh, and a
# package missing from it fails SILENTLY: apk simply never offers the newer
# version, so the device holds the old one and every UI says "up to date". That
# is how device r80 shipped against a missing nexusq-rootfs-ab. A second copy of
# the list in the gate would reproduce the same trap one level up — a gate that
# checks the subset it happens to know about is a gate that agrees with the bug.
#
# ADDING A PACKAGE: any new runtime dependency of something already here belongs
# here too, or apk resolves the upgrade against a dependency it cannot fetch and
# holds the whole transaction back.
#
# NOT here, deliberately:
#   nexusq-glibc-rt   ~180 MB static Roon base — over GitHub's 100 MB limit,
#                     flash-only. It changes about never.
#   the kernel itself is here only as a PAYLOAD (see linux-google-steelhead
#   below), never as something apk installs.

nexusq-control
nexusqd
nexusq-btagent
nexusq-setupd
nexusq-mqtt
nexusq-kernel-ota
nexusq-rootfs-ab

# A payload source for nq-kernel-ota, NOT an installable: apk never applies a
# kernel. nexusq-control upgrades with `--ignore linux-google-steelhead`, and
# nq-kernel-ota fetches this apk, unpacks it and writes a boot image to the
# trial slot. docs/2026-08-18-kernel-ota-phase2.md
linux-google-steelhead

# Re-enabled 2026-08-30 (r91) after the reason for holding it back was removed.
# Up to r90 this package INSTALLED the device's access files — the WiFi profile
# with the WPA PSK in plain text and two authorized_keys — so publishing it put
# them on a public branch (r62..r90). From r91 the package ships none of them:
# docker-build.sh writes them straight into the rootfs at the end of Phase 10,
# unowned by apk, so a fresh flash still comes up reachable.
#
# Boxes already in the field are carried across by the package's .pre-upgrade /
# .post-upgrade pair, because apk DELETES files that leave a package's file list
# and an unguarded r90 -> r91 upgrade would take a device's WiFi profile and root
# authorized_keys with it. Tested in pmos/device-google-steelhead/tests/
# test_access_migration.sh, including watching it fail without the migration.
device-google-steelhead
device-google-steelhead-nonfree-firmware

# Not one of ours by name — a version-pinned OVERRIDE of Alpine's package,
# rebuilt with NEON (pmos/speexdsp/APKBUILD). It must be published like any
# other, or a device that OTA-upgrades keeps Alpine's SCALAR build and silently
# loses the resampler win.
speexdsp
